// village_economy noncombat acceptance: bilateral consent + obligation
// pair. The dispatcher walks the program and writes:
//   * EffectProposeApplied         (kind=73) — Lift C: caster offers a
//                                   bilateral agreement of kind=4
//                                   (Service) to the cast target;
//                                   expires_at_tick=200 (test horizon).
//   * EffectCreateObligationApplied (kind=76) — Lift D: caster registers
//                                   obligation slot id=1, kind=0
//                                   (Debt) against the cast target.
//
// Together this pair pins the consent + persistent-record surfaces:
// caster proposes a service deal AND records the implied debt in one
// cast. In the full economy these would split (a target-side accept
// gate would materialize the debt only after acceptance), but for the
// foundation acceptance fixture both records flow through the same
// cast — exercising the lift surface end-to-end without yet shipping
// the accept / decline / discharge companion verbs.
//
// `target: enemy` is the only non-self ability target in this fixture
// (recipes/wear/skills/announces are all self-cast). The runtime test
// pins this by checking that obligation/proposal records carry distinct
// caster_slot != target_slot.

ability OfferDeal {
    target: enemy
    range: 100.0
    cooldown: 5s
    hint: utility

    propose 4 expires_at 200 [UTILITY: 100]
    create_obligation 1 0 [UTILITY: 100]
}
